{% comment %}
  Half vertical — 400x480 on an OG. Width is the constraint here, not height:
  the panel is as tall as the full view, so all six rows still fit. What has
  to go is the HI / LO column. The end dot stays: it is a <circle> in the
  unscaled outer svg, so the viewBox squashing x cannot turn it into an
  ellipse (see shared.liquid).
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
    THE TYPE SCALE
    The pair is `value--xxsmall`, the framework's 16px bitmap tier on a 1-bit
    panel, and the rate `value--xsmall` (20px Inter): the smallest pair of
    tiers that still reads as pair-then-rate. The change is a plain `label`
    pill, without the full view's extra padding, which this width cannot
    afford. A TRMNL X steps each up one (`lg:value--xsmall`,
    `lg:value--small`, `lg:label--large`), which is what fills its panel.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    THE TRACKS
    Every pair is exactly XXX -> XXX, so the first column's width is fixed.
    The change track is the pill at its widest (`+1235%`). TREND is the last
    column, so the trace cell keeps the end dot's overhang inside it (`pr--1`).
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    PORTRAIT ON A TRMNL X: TWO LINES PER ROW
    390px. As in the full view: pair, rate and change on one line, the rate
    right-aligned against the pill, and the trace across the full width
    beneath (`portrait:col--span-3`). The header has the trend label on a
    second, smaller line at the trace's left edge.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    PORTRAIT ON AN OG: NO HEADER
    240px, of which 205 are usable. Four header labels in that width were
    clutter, and a pair, a rate, a signed percentage and a trace need no
    labels at this size. So the header is hidden (`portrait:hidden`, brought
    back for the X by `lg:portrait:grid`), the row is pair and rate on one
    line with the pill and the trace on the next, the pill at the left edge
    under the pair, and the height the header took goes to the traces. The
    window the header named moves to the title bar, in the range setting's
    own short form: `1Y to 25 Sep 2026`.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    THE PLOT HEIGHT
    (box - chrome) / 6 - inset, with no cap: six rows fill every device. The
    row inset is `py--4`. See full.liquid for the terms. On an OG in portrait
    there is no header, and the chrome term is negative: the rows are budgeted
    to run a few px into the layout's bottom padding, which is still clear of
    the title bar.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    THE RATE TRACK IS CUT TO THE LONGEST RATE ON SHOW
    Each row is its own grid, so a track that sized to its content would put
    the pill and the trace of a long-rate row (JPY -> USD is `0.0063521`, nine
    characters) to the right of every other row's. The track is therefore a
    fixed width, and since width is what this view is short of, it is the
    width of the longest rate in these rows rather than of the longest rate
    possible: tabular figures run 13px a character at the OG tier and 17px at
    the X's, less the narrower point. Seven characters is the floor (`0.82829`),
    so the track does not move when a rate crosses 1.
  {% endcomment %}
{% assign fx_rate_chars = 7 %}
{% for row in rows limit: 6 %}{% assign fx_n = row.rate_str | size %}{% if fx_n > fx_rate_chars %}{% assign fx_rate_chars = fx_n %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% assign fx_rate_w = fx_rate_chars | times: 13 | minus: 5 %}
{% assign fx_rate_w_lg = fx_rate_chars | times: 17 | minus: 7 %}
{% comment %}
    THE WINDOW IS SHORTENED WHERE ITS NAME IS TOO LONG FOR THE TRACE TRACK
    The trend header sits over a track about 100px wide in landscape. "1 YEAR
    TREND" and "5 YEARS TREND" fit it; "3 MONTHS TREND" and "6 MONTHS TREND"
    do not, and a header that wraps to a second line pushes the last row into
    the title bar. Those two print as "3M TREND" and "6M TREND", the form the
    narrow portrait title bar already uses.
  {% endcomment %}
{% assign fx_window = range_label %}
{% if range_label.size > 7 %}{% assign fx_range = range_label | split: " " %}{% capture fx_window %}{{ fx_range[0] }}{{ fx_range[1] | slice: 0 }}{% endcapture %}{% endif %}
{% comment %}
    THE PAIR TRACK UNDER A PINNED TEXT SCALE
    80px holds XXX -> XXX in the OG's pixel font. With Text Scale at large or
    x-large the size is held at regular (shared.liquid) but the OG is on Inter,
    where the same pair is up to 88px. The track is 88px there and no more:
    the 8px comes off the trace track, and "5 YEARS TREND" needs 94 of the 96
    that leaves in landscape. A wider pair runs into the gap, not the rate.
  {% endcomment %}
<style>
  .fx--halfv { --fx-pair: 80px; }
  .screen--md.screen--text-scale-large .fx--halfv,
  .screen--md.screen--text-scale-xlarge .fx--halfv { --fx-pair: 88px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: var(--fx-pair) {{ fx_rate_w }}px 70px 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: 112px {{ fx_rate_w_lg }}px 95px 1fr; }
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: 112px 1fr 95px; }
  .screen--md.screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .screen--md.screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: var(--fx-pair) 1fr; }
  .screen--md.screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-spark { grid-column: auto; }
  .screen--md.screen--portrait .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: -18px; }
  .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 26px; --fx-inset: 33px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 34px; }
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 48px; --fx-inset: 70px; }
  .screen--lg.screen--portrait .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 36px; --fx-inset: 74px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-dot  { r: 3px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-dot { r: 4px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-spark svg { height: calc((100cqh - var(--fx-chrome)) / 6 - var(--fx-inset)); }
</style>

<div class="layout layout--col layout--justify-start fx-box">
  {% if fx_failed %}
    <div class="fx-error flex flex--col flex--center-y text--center">
      <span class="title">Rates unavailable</span>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="fx-list flex flex--col gap--none pt--2.5 fx--halfv">
      <div class="fx-head grid pb--1 portrait:hidden lg:portrait:grid">
        <div class="flex gap--none"><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base">PAIR</span></div><div class="flex flex--right gap--none"><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base">LATEST</span></div><div class="flex flex--right gap--none"><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base">CHANGE</span></div><div class="fx-trend flex flex--center-x portrait:flex--left gap--none portrait:col--span-3"><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base lg:portrait:label--small">{% if range_label %}{{ fx_window }} {% endif %}TREND</span></div>
      </div>

      {% for row in rows limit: 6 %}
        <div class="fx-row grid py--4">
          <div class="fx-pair value value--xxsmall text--bold lg:value--xsmall">{{ row.from }}<span class="fx-arrow text--regular px--0.5">&rarr;</span>{{ row.to }}</div>
          <div class="fx-rate value value--xsmall value--tnums text--bold lg:value--small text--right">{{ row.rate_str }}</div>
          <div class="fx-chg flex flex--right portrait:flex--left lg:portrait:flex--right gap--none"><span class="label text--bold value--tnums lg:label--large {% if row.change_pct < 0 %}label--filled{% else %}label--outline{% endif %}">{{ row.change_str | replace: "-", "&minus;" }}%</span></div>
          {% assign fx_end = row.points | split: " " | last | split: "," %}
          {% assign fx_end_y = fx_end[1] | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 30 %}
          <div class="fx-spark flex gap--none pr--1 portrait:col--span-3">
            <svg class="fx-plot block" width="100%" height="24">
              <svg class="block" viewBox="0 0 200 30" width="100%" height="100%" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                <polyline points="{{ row.points }}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
              </svg>
              <circle class="fx-dot" cx="100%" cy="{{ fx_end_y }}%"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% comment %}
  The title bar has half a panel's width at most, which the full window
  (`26 Sep 2025 - 25 Sep 2026`) does not fit, so it carries the as-of date
  alone: the header already names the window. On an OG in portrait there is no
  header and no room for the title either, so the title is hidden and the date
  is prefixed with the window in short form (`1Y`, from the range label).
{% endcomment %}
<div class="title_bar">
  {{ fx_icon }}
  <span class="title portrait:hidden lg:portrait:inline">Exchange Rates{% if env %} ({{ env | upcase }}){% endif %}</span>
  <span class="instance">{% if fx_failed %}No data{% else %}<span class="fx-dates text--default">{% if range_label %}{% assign fx_range = range_label | split: " " %}<span class="hidden portrait:inline lg:portrait:hidden">{{ fx_range[0] }}{{ fx_range[1] | slice: 0 }} to </span>{% endif %}{{ as_of | date: "%-d %b %Y" }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
</div>
